      "pText": "Udanchu is a giant fly scaled up for children to climb, with net wings on either side of a Play Yellow body and a yellow slide. Children climb over the wings and look closely at their patterns, then slide down from the top. The design asks children to notice and observe small creatures. School-age children from 5 to 12 use it, up to 15 together. The product area is 10' x 14'10\" and the safe play area is 16' x 17'10\", a compact size for a school garden or nature trail. Climbing, hanging and sliding build upper body strength, coordination and parallel play. A 3-year warranty covers the galvanised pipe, roto-moulded parts, composite laminates and play rope. Call +91 902 830 2266 for a layout drawing."
